{title: I’ve got joy}
{x_theme: joy, grace-mercy, praise, heaven, victory}
{x_source: docx:1. Incomplete/I_ve got joy.docx}

{comment: Verse 1}
Maybe you can tell it by the smile on my face
I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy
It’s a joy that comes from Heaven that the world cannot erase
I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy
When I rise in the morning, see the day God has made
Sunshine or storming you’ll still hear me say
I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy.

{comment: Verse 2}
When trouble’s all around me I can sing amazing grace
I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy
Problems cannot stop me, I’m gonna win this race.
I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy
He’s strength to my spirit, provider and friend
I can’t help but shout it and say it again,
I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy.

{comment: Bridge}
This joy is not dependent on what I feel or see.
No matter what the struggle I still have victory.
There’s joy for my journey no man can take away.
The joy of the Lord is my strength today.

{comment: Verse 3}
Now Jesus is the solid rock I’m standing on today.
I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy
He has taken all my burdens and He’s washed my sins away.
I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy
Sunshine or storming you’ll still hear me say
I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy, I’ve got joy.
